  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You receive an array `prices` where `prices[i]` is the price of a given stock on the `ith` day.\n\nIdentify the largest profit you can achieve. You may complete **no more than two transactions**.\n\n**Note:** You may not engage in multiple transactions simultaneously (i.e., you must sell the stock before you buy again).\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: prices = [3,3,5,0,0,3,1,4]\nOutput: 6\nExplanation: Buy on day 4 (price = 0) and sell on day 6 (price = 3), profit = 3-0 = 3.\nThen buy on day 7 (price = 1) and sell on day 8 (price = 4), profit = 4-1 = 3.\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: prices = [1,2,3,4,5]\nOutput: 4\nExplanation: Buy on day 1 (price = 1) and sell on day 5 (price = 5), profit = 5-1 = 4.\nNote that you cannot buy on day 1, buy on day 2 and sell them later, as you are engaging multiple transactions at the same time. You must sell before buying again.\n```\n\n**Example 3:**\n\n```\nInput: prices = [7,6,4,3,1]\nOutput: 0\nExplanation: In this case, no transaction is done, i.e. max profit = 0.\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= prices.length <= 105`\n* `0 <= prices[i] <= 105`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
